g tests for the new argv and prompt shape.\n- Update `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md` to drop the stale \"rejects an additional prompt\" claim and document the codex version requirement.\n- One commit per user's \"few commits per PR\" preference.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, `exec.Cmd`, codex CLI ≥ 0.130.0 (this is what's installed locally — earlier versions of `codex exec review` did not accept `[PROMPT]`).\n\n---\n\n## Pre-flight\n\n- [ ] **Confirm branch and codex version**\n\n  Run:\n  ```bash\n  git branch --show-current\n  codex --version\n  codex exec review --help 2>&1 | head -5\n  ```\n  Expected:\n  - Branch: `slow-codex-in-review` (or whatever feature branch the work happens on)\n  - codex-cli ≥ 0.130.0\n  - `Usage: codex exec review [OPTIONS] [PROMPT]` appears in the help\n\n- [ ] **Confirm `mise run check` baseline is clean before any edits**\n\n  Run: `mise run check`\n  Expected: PASS. If it fails before any change, fix or note the unrelated failure first — we want a clean baseline so the post-edit run is interpretable.\n\n---\n\n## Task 1: Codex-specific prompt composer\n\nThe new composer drops `/review` (handled by the subcommand) and the explicit scope clause (handled by `--base` / `--uncommitted` flags). It keeps non-`/review` skills, always-prompt, per-run-prompt, and checkpoint context.\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/prompt.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/prompt_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\n  Create `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/prompt_test.go`:\n\n  ```go\n  package codex\n\n  import (\n      \"strings\"\n      \"testing\"\n\n      reviewtypes \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/types\"\n  )\n\n  func TestComposeNativeReviewPrompt_DropsBuiltinReview(t *testing.T) {\n      t.Parallel()\n      cfg := reviewtypes.RunConfig{Skills: []string{\"/review\"}}\n      got := composeNativeReviewPrompt(cfg)\n      if strings.Contains(got, \"/review\") {\n          t.Fatalf(\"prompt must not contain /review:\\n%s\", got)\n      }\n      if strings.Contains(got, \"Review the current branch changes\") {\n          t.Fatalf(\"prompt must not contain stale paraphrase:\\n%s\", got)\n      }\n  }\n\n  func TestComposeNativeReviewPrompt_DropsExplicitScopeClause(t *testing.T) {\n      t.Parallel()\n      cfg := reviewtypes.RunConfig{\n          Skills:       []string{\"/review\"},\n          ScopeBaseRef: \"main\",\n      }\n      got := composeNativeReviewPrompt(cfg)\n      if strings.Contains(got, \"Scope:\") {\n          t.Fatalf(\"prompt must not contain explicit Scope clause (flags carry it):\\n%s\", got)\n      }\n  }\n\n  func TestComposeNativeReviewPrompt_KeepsOtherContext(t *testing.T) {\n      t.Parallel()\n      cfg := reviewtypes.RunConfig{\n          Skills:            []string{\"/review\", \"/some-other-skill\"},\n          AlwaysPrompt:      \"Always check error handling.\",\n          PerRunPrompt:      \"Focus on the storage layer.\",\n          ScopeBaseRef:      \"main\",\n          CheckpointContext: \"Commits in scope:\\n  abc123 summary\\n\",\n      }\n      got := composeNativeReviewPrompt(cfg)\n      for _, want := range []string{\n          \"/some-other-skill\",\n          \"Always check error handling.\",\n          \"Focus on the storage layer.\",\n          \"Commits in scope:\",\n          \"abc123 summary\",\n      } {\n          if !strings.Contains(got, want) {\n              t.Errorf(\"prompt missing %q:\\n%s\", want, got)\n          }\n      }\n  }\n\n  func TestComposeNativeReviewPrompt_PromptOverridePassesThrough(t *testing.T) {\n      t.Parallel()\n      cfg := reviewtypes.RunConfig{PromptOverride: \"literal override\"}\n      got := composeNativeReviewPrompt(cfg)\n      if got != \"literal override\" {\n          t.Errorf(\"PromptOverride should bypass composition, got %q\", got)\n      }\n  }\n  ```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\n  Run: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/ -run TestComposeNativeReviewPrompt -v`\n  Expected: FAIL with \"undefined: composeNativeReviewPrompt\"\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement minimal composer**\n\n  Create `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/prompt.go`:\n\n  ```go\n  package codex\n\n  import (\n      \"strings\"\n\n      reviewtypes \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/types\"\n  )\n\n  // composeNativeReviewPrompt builds the stdin payload for `codex exec review -`.\n  // It mirrors review.ComposeReviewPrompt but drops the two pieces that\n  // `codex exec review` now handles natively:\n  //\n  //  1. The `/review` skill invocation — the subcommand IS the review.\n  //  2. The explicit \"Scope: ...\" clause — `--base` / `--uncommitted` flags\n  //     carry scope authoritatively.\n  //\n  // PromptOverride bypasses composition for callers that need verbatim control.\n  func composeNativeReviewPrompt(cfg reviewtypes.RunConfig) string {\n      if cfg.PromptOverride != \"\" {\n          return cfg.PromptOverride\n      }\n\n      var sections []string\n\n      // Skills, minus /review (handled by `exec review` subcommand).\n      filtered := filterOutBuiltinReview(cfg.Skills)\n      if len(filtered) > 0 {\n          sections = append(sections, strings.Join(filtered, \"\\n\"))\n      }\n\n      if trimmed := strings.TrimRight(cfg.AlwaysPrompt, \"\\n\\r \"); trimmed != \"\" {\n          sections = append(sections, trimmed)\n      }\n      if trimmed := strings.TrimRight(cfg.PerRunPrompt, \"\\n\\r \"); trimmed != \"\" {\n          sections = append(sections, trimmed)\n      }\n      // NB: no explicit Scope clause here — codex `--base` / `--uncommitted` flags\n      // are the authoritative source. The redundant clause confused codex's\n      // exec-mode reasoning loop and was a contributor to the 2-5x speed gap.\n\n      if trimmed := strings.TrimRight(cfg.CheckpointContext, \"\\n\\r \"); trimmed != \"\" {\n          sections = append(sections, trimmed)\n      }\n      return strings.Join(sections, \"\\n\\n\")\n  }\n\n  // filterOutBuiltinReview removes the literal `/review` token from a skills\n  // list. Other skill invocations pass through verbatim — codex picker only\n  // offers `/review` today (DiscoverReviewSkills is stubbed), so this is a\n  // future-compat hedge for when plugin discovery lands.\n  func filterOutBuiltinReview(skills []string) []string {\n      out := make([]string, 0, len(skills))\n      for _, s := range skills {\n          if s == \"/review\" {\n              continue\n          }\n          out = append(out, s)\n      }\n      return out\n  }\n  ```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run test to verify it passes**\n\n  Run: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/ -run TestComposeNativeReviewPrompt -v`\n  Expected: PASS (all 4 cases)\n\n---\n\n## Task 2: Switch `buildCodexReviewCmd` argv to `exec review`\n\nReplace the `exec --skip-git-repo-check -` argv with `exec review [--base <ref>] --uncommitted --json --skip-git-repo-check -`. Replace the call to `review.ComposeReviewPrompt` with the new `composeNativeReviewPrompt`.\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer.go:30-41` (and surrounding comment)\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer_test.go:69-125` (argv + paraphrase tests)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Update argv shape test to expect new shape**\n\n  In `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer_test.go`, replace the body of `TestCodexReviewer_ArgvShape` (currently lines 69-88) with:\n\n  ```go\n  func TestCodexReviewer_ArgvShape_WithBaseRef(t *testing.T) {\n      t.Parallel()\n      cfg := reviewtypes.RunConfig{\n          Skills:       []string{\"/review\"},\n          ScopeBaseRef: \"main\",\n      }\n      cmd := buildCodexReviewCmd(context.Background(), cfg)\n\n      // Expect: codex exec review --base main --uncommitted --json --skip-git-repo-check -\n      want := []string{\n          wantCodexAgentName, \"exec\", \"review\",\n          \"--base\", \"main\",\n          \"--uncommitted\",\n          \"--json\",\n          \"--skip-git-repo-check\", \"-