{"parentUuid":"0003bd48-4746-42b4-ba2e-7353e382d215","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"930d1f5f-2d4d-4177-8d7c-89f69eea67af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014uiKZFhCaFRLbMmjK9wEdf","type":"tool_result","content":"===CLAUDE output (last 60 lines)===\nThe reviewer test `TestCodexReviewer_CustomizationPropagatedViaEnv` sets `PerRunPrompt` and asserts `EnvPrompt != \"\"` but never asserts the per-run text is recoverable — so the bug is invisible to the test suite.\n### 2. **The whole hook-injection path only works when `codex_hooks` is enabled — and `codex exec review` may not fire user-prompt-submit at all** (silent failure surface)\n`AGENT.md:220` (in this branch, unchanged) says:\n> Hooks require feature flag: The `codex_hooks` feature is `default_enabled: false` (stage: UnderDevelopment). … Without this, hooks.json is ignored entirely.\n`buildCodexReviewCmd` does not pass `-c features.codex_hooks=true` (now: `hooks=true` per `hooks.go:353`), so the spawned codex inherits whatever's in the user's project/global config. `entire enable` writes that flag for users who go through the enable flow, but `entire review --agent codex` can be run in arbitrary repos and the env-var → hook → additionalContext chain depends on a feature flag the review command never asserts.\nWorse: even with the feature flag on, there's no evidence in this PR that `codex exec review` (the subcommand) fires the `user-prompt-submit` hook at all. The hook name strongly suggests interactive prompt submission, not subcommand-driven runs. There is no e2e test, no captured-stdout fixture, and no citation showing this hook fires during `exec review`.\nIf either condition fails, the model sees only codex's stock `/review` curated prompt and the user's always-prompt / per-run prompt / checkpoint context / non-`/review` skills are all silently dropped — with the env vars set, hook registered, code building cleanly, and tests passing. This is the worst category of sil