 echo \"===Codex first-line (PR)===\" ; grep -m1 -o '\\\"text\\\":\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"' /tmp/pr.txt | head -c 300; echo; echo; echo \"===Codex first-line (MAIN)===\"; grep -m1 -o '\\\"text\\\":\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"' /tmp/main.txt | head -c 300; echo\n```\n\nAfter it finishes you'll see:\n- Wall-clock per agent\n- Marker hit counts per agent (any > 0 = always-prompt reached the model)\n- Codex's first assistant line on each binary — **this is the qualitative diagnostic**:\n  - **PR binary**: should mention `code-reviewer` skill explicitly (codex saw `/review`, routed to your installed skill)\n  - **Main binary**: should be generic instruction text (codex received the paraphrase, not the slash-command)\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nRunning them in parallel saves wall-clock time, but you lose live UX visibility. For the *qualitative* part of \"is this fix doing what I think?\", running one foreground (recipe A) and watching codex's first assistant line is more revealing than the parallel comparison's grep output. Codex saying \"Using `code-reviewer`...\" on the PR binary vs. \"Reviewing changes...\" on main is the smoking gun for the prompt-passes-through behavior change.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nWant me to also create a small shell script you can save and run, so you don't need to paste a long one-liner each time?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4467,"cache_read_input_tokens":599425,"output_tokens":3858,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4467,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3858,"cache_read_input_tokens":599425,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4467},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},